{
  "abstract": "Motivated by Alpöge's generic-degree-three counterexample to JC(3), we formalize the collision geometry of complex three-dimensional Keller maps of that degree. Using classical Keller–Galois rigidity, we identify the residual generic collision factor with the normal closure of the induced function-field extension, whose Galois group is S3. The decomposition separates the diagonal and proves nonvanishing of the collision obstruction.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Chloe van der Vlugt"
    }
  ],
